            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><h3><span>Father’s Day Car Show</span></h3>
<p>Sunday, June 21 from 10 am to 3 pm<br><span>Cost: Single admission - $8.93; Family admission (two adults and accompanying children from the same household) - $23.15.</span></p>
<p><span>Treat your dad, paternal role model, or favourite car enthusiast to a day of family-friendly fun at Billings Estate National Historic Site. Chat with community members about their pre-1999&nbsp;antique and vintage cars. The Billings’ 1959 Cadillac Sedan de Ville will also be on display. Cast a vote for your favourite car, explore the museum at Ottawa’s oldest wood frame house, and challenge each other to a scavenger hunt.</span></p>
<h4><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">Participate in the&nbsp;car&nbsp;show</span><span>&nbsp;</span></h4>
<p><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">Car owners are invited to&nbsp;participate&nbsp;in the Father’s Day Car Show at Billings Estate National Historic Site with their pre-1999&nbsp;vehicles (no&nbsp;‘mods’&nbsp;or hot&nbsp;rods).&nbsp;<strong>To&nbsp;participate, please complete the </strong></span><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/forms/fathers-day-car-show-registration"><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr"><strong>online registration form</strong></span></a><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr"><strong>&nbsp;by&nbsp;June&nbsp;19, 2026.</strong></span>&nbsp;</p>
<p>P<span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">lan to arrive at the museum (2100 Cabot Street) on&nbsp;June 21&nbsp;between 8:30 am and 9:45&nbsp;am. Staff will direct you to assigned parking (based on order of arrival). We hope that you will be able to&nbsp;participate&nbsp;for the duration of the event. If you need to&nbsp;depart&nbsp;early, we&nbsp;request&nbsp;that you&nbsp;depart&nbsp;on the hour so we can coordinate the movement of vehicles.&nbsp;Registered car owners will receive&nbsp;up to&nbsp;two&nbsp;meal&nbsp;chits&nbsp;per vehicle&nbsp;for lunch.</span>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">If you have questions, contact  </span><a href="mailto:larysa.voss@ottawa.ca"><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">larysa.voss@ottawa.ca</span></a><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">.</span>&nbsp;</p>
<h4><strong>Notes</strong></h4>
<ul>
<li><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">This program takes place rain or shine. Please dress for weather conditions, including proper footwear for uneven, grassy, or gravel terrain.</span></li>
<li><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">As many of the vehicles are owned by community members, the number of participating vehicles may vary throughout the day (or be&nbsp;impacted&nbsp;by inclement weather).</span></li>
<li><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">If you have questions or concerns&nbsp;regarding&nbsp;accessibility, please contact the museum at 613-580-2088 or by email&nbsp;at </span><a href="mailto:museums@ottawa.ca"><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">museums@ottawa.ca</span></a><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">.&nbsp;Additional </span><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/place-listing/billings-estate-national-historic-site#section-fc740f5f-d58b-44aa-a647-439ad640a60f"><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr">information about accessibility</span></a><span lang="EN-CA" dir="ltr"> can be found on the museum webpage.</span>&nbsp;</li>
</ul></div>
      
