            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><h3>Mother's Day Tea</h3>
<p>Sunday, May 10&nbsp;with seatings at 10:30 am, 12:30 pm and 2:30 pm&nbsp;<br>Cost:&nbsp;$32.99&nbsp;per person (taxes included)&nbsp;<br><strong>Reservations are&nbsp;required.</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Share&nbsp;a&nbsp;delicious three-tier&nbsp;tea&nbsp;service&nbsp;with your loved ones while enjoying the&nbsp;beautiful grounds and gardens at Billings Estate National Historic Site.&nbsp;Following tea, step inside Ottawa’s oldest wood-framed house to learn more about the Billings family and explore&nbsp;the special exhibition,&nbsp;<em>Beyond the Brim: Tales Told Through the Hats We Wore.</em>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The tea service includes a pot of tea, finger sandwiches, a scone with butter and&nbsp;jam&nbsp;and a&nbsp;selection&nbsp;of mini desserts. All menu items are prepared or baked in-house with fresh ingredients.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Reservations</h4>
<p><span><strong>The reservation request form for Mother’s Day Tea is now closed.</strong> Thank you for your patience as we process and respond to the reservation requests. If you submitted a request, a member of our team will follow up with you via email. We anticipate sending these emails by Monday, March 30 at 5 pm.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><strong>Notes:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>We&nbsp;anticipate&nbsp;interest in this program will exceed capacity and that reservations will fill quickly.&nbsp;In&nbsp;past years we have stopped&nbsp;accepting reservation requests before noon on the&nbsp;same&nbsp;day the form opens. Regrettably, we&nbsp;can’t&nbsp;guarantee that everyone&nbsp;who&nbsp;submits&nbsp;a request will be successful in securing a reservation.</li>
<li>Reservations are filled in the&nbsp;order&nbsp;requests are received.&nbsp;Submitting the request form does not confirm your booking. A staff person will follow up with you by&nbsp;email to review your request and to provide further details&nbsp;regarding&nbsp;advance payment.</li>
<li>Your reservation is not confirmed until advance payment is received.&nbsp;If advance payment is not received by the communicated date, the reservation will be offered to the next&nbsp;client&nbsp;on the waitlist.</li>
<li>A waitlist will be&nbsp;maintained&nbsp;once reservations are full.&nbsp;We encourage&nbsp;clients&nbsp;to also consider our&nbsp;Tea on the Lawn&nbsp;service. Tea on the Lawn is offered from&nbsp;May 15 to August 30. The online reservation request form for Tea on the Lawn&nbsp;opens&nbsp;Tuesday, April 14 at 10 am.</li>
<li>The maximum reservation size is six guests.</li>
<li>Guests are seated at tables in groups of four or six.&nbsp;To ensure pathways are clear, tables cannot be pushed&nbsp;together,&nbsp;and&nbsp;additional&nbsp;chairs cannot be added to a table.</li>
<li>Pairs and smaller groups will be seated at a shared table.&nbsp;We encourage guests to&nbsp;break the ice and&nbsp;enjoy conversation with their&nbsp;tablemates&nbsp;over a cup of tea.</li>
<li><strong>Mother’s Day&nbsp;Tea is served outdoors under the cover of a tent.</strong>&nbsp;Please dress for the weather, including appropriate footwear for grassy terrain.&nbsp;&nbsp;Mother’s Day Tea will run as scheduled in most weather conditions. However, in the rare event that weather conditions or other unforeseen circumstances necessitate the cancellation of this event, all guests with a reservation will be contacted directly with further information.</li>
<li>We&nbsp;will inquire about food allergies and dietary restrictions when confirming your reservation.&nbsp;<strong>Vegan and gluten-free alternatives are available but must be requested in advance.</strong>&nbsp;Please review any individual needs with every member of your group before booking. While we make reasonable efforts to accommodate allergies and dietary restrictions identified during the reservation process, we cannot guarantee a cross-contact free environment.&nbsp;We are unable to meet last-minute requests for accommodation at the time of service.</li>
<li><strong>We will inquire about any&nbsp;accessibility needs when confirming your reservation.&nbsp;</strong>There are two tents for Mother’s Day Tea. The first is accessed by a paved pathway and has a stone floor. The second has a grass floor and&nbsp;is accessed by crossing the lawn. A passenger drop-off and pick-up&nbsp;zone is available in front of&nbsp;the lobby&nbsp;entrance&nbsp;and parking is available on site. The special exhibition,&nbsp;<em>Beyond the Brim,</em>&nbsp;is located on the second floor of the museum and is accessible by stairs only.&nbsp;A visual guide will be available for visitors who cannot access the&nbsp;second floor.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>
